    "configure": "process.terminal.configure requires execute, a complete six-flag/seven-byte record and expected desired revision. CAS publishes the new desired state; every accepted call advances revision, including identical attributes.",
    "observe": "process.terminal.attributes requires read and timeoutMs 0..25000. The native feeder observes through one pending R2 epoch shared by concurrent readers. Queued/parked processes time out without an invented native snapshot.",
    "state": "One version-3 input head retains desired state, observation epochs and optional final snapshot alongside existing bytes, EOF and geometry. Rust owns current attributes and applied revision.",
    "recovery": "Same retained revision preserves later guest tcsetattr changes and child restore frames after same-build heap restoration. A new desired revision supersedes older raw restoration.",
    "settlement": "Actual native completion and active cancellation retain final attributes after raw-owner cleanup. Repeated settled reads do not write; configure rejects settlement. Cancelled-before-entry or historical jobs without native snapshots cannot return fabricated attributes.",
    "migration": "Alchemy unconditionally runs input-terminal-v3. Both historical versions convert under ETags, retaining bytes, EOF and version-2 geometry. Current heads skip writes."
  },
